  + a concurrent local Windows focused-test and Clippy attempt caused Application Control to refuse the freshly rebuilt semantic_anchor_scan executable with OS error 4551 before tests executed
  + the same attempt exposed one Clippy collapsible_if style finding which was corrected
  + no Rust assertion failure occurred and the operational fault is preserved under narrative/operational_faults
  + the authoritative serial WSL rerun executed all fourteen scanner tests and all workspace tests with zero failure without changing host policy or privileges

& [ReviewCorrections]
  + an initial immutable-borrow ambiguity marker was replaced with an owned tier value before tests
  + byte clipping was hardened to forbid an empty page whose cursor would not advance
  + future applicability candidates require exact operation-index and identity-entry address equality
  + candidate accumulation was bounded before output construction so query budgets govern discovery work rather than JSON alone

